cture of what you need to  accomplish  another common practice is to always set  deadlines for your objectives  this acts as a motivator and encourages  you to work hard this will also help you  to establish a better work life balance  and feel more in control over the flow  of your life day-to-day  setting both short and long-term goals  as well as a well-thought-out plan to  reach them is a smart idea and it's a  very good start when it comes to  building your self-discipline  it is the driving force that helps to  catapult individuals out of the  mediocrity and into better lives for  themselves and their loved ones  it doesn't have to strictly apply to  academics or career growth either it can  also apply to social and relationship  development as well as one's health  for example when looking to get into  better shape many give up or don't even  start because they fear it may be too  difficult or drastic of a change to  strive for  those with strong self-discipline as  well as encouragement for their friends  and family tend to have much more  success in doing this but most of them  don't  they'll be more likely to stick to a  diet instead of cheating and to  establish a workout schedule to better  themselves physically and the result is  that these people end up living happier  healthier day after day and end up also  living more confidently  this also gives the feeling that they  have control over themselves their mind  their bodies and their lives  as touched on briefly self-discipline  ties in heavily with  self-control which in itself it's not  just a form of control  the reason why so many people struggle  with self-discipline is that we live in  a society where people are gradually  losing the ability to think for  themselves  and make their own informed decisions  this is something that ties in with the  world of technology as well  let's take our social media for example  those have definitely a  those have a bad influence on our  uh process of building a self-esteem and  also building uh the self-discipline  that we are  trying to achieve as one of our  monthly or yearly goals  we have grown accustomed to relying on  lock down walled garden products and  services that are designed to limit the  control of the consumer  or to reduce the amount of decisions  consumers have to make for themselves  in a nutshell indoctrinating the next  generation to simply do as they're told  and not look into things not think them  through or  have a critical thinking process on  deciding something  uh whether it's something you want to  buy in in a  in a shop or  whether it's something you want to buy a  new cell phone a new product whatever  that  advertisements are showing up in your on  your screen  not having to think for themselves and  make their own decisions is actually  something that many people find  a sense of comfort in  they're content with mediocrity they  don't see a reason for anything to  change because in their eyes it's uh  good enough  this is also very similar to how many  former prisoners believe  that they found a sense of comfort in  not having to make their own decisions  or make their own money or make their  own life work again  albeit not a great situation to be in  they were  i mean a lot of prisoners were  guaranteed a living space and three  meals a day  as a society over time we have  sacrificed a rapidly increasing number  of our freedoms and our control over our  own lives for convenience and this sense  of stability  um  finally in my opinion  when we are self-disciplined we are also  very proactive in making the decisions  that will ultimately benefit us in the  long term the common expression lazy  people work twice as hard  is more factual than many may realize  those who are content with mediocrity  and do not push themselves to break out  a little harder  tend to stay there the longest it is  only when we as people begin to take  control of our own lives  our own habits our own thoughts and our  own small acts of kindness that we begin  to find success  and the good things in life will not  just come to you they say that the  pieces are already there for you and  it's up to you  and it's up to us  to find them and put them together  and uh this is all for today  if you really like this episode make  sure to check out our channel for other  similar episodes about very interesting  topics  and to subscribe to our channel  thank you for listening  [Music]  you

